===Noun===
{{en-noun|millennia|s}}

# A [[period]] of [[time]] consisting of one thousand [[year]]s.
#: {{coord|en|annum|biennium|triennium|quadrennium|quinquennium|sexennium|septennium|octennium|novennium|decennium|vicennium|tricennium|centennium|quincentennium|decamillennium|centimillennium|millionennium}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1968|author={{w|Joseph Campbell}}|title={{w|The Hero with a Thousand Faces}}|year_published=1993|location=London|publisher=Fontana Press|edition=2nd|page=23|passage=But these seekers, too, are saved - by virtue of the inherited symbolic aids of society, the rites of passage, the grace-yielding sacraments, given to mankind of old by the redeemers and handed down through '''millenniums'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2013
|author=w:Al Gore
|title={{w|The Future: Six Drivers of Global Change}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/futuresixdrivers0000gore_k5o2/
|location=[[New York]]
|publisher=w:Random House
|ISBN=978-0-8129-9294-6
|LCCN=2012039890
|OCLC=827202765
|page=37
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/futuresixdrivers0000gore_k5o2/page/37/
|text=The first known man-made tools, including spear points and axes, were associated with a hunting and gathering pattern that lasted, according to anthropologists, almost 200 '''millennia'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=24 March 2013|author=Dan Pearson|work=The Guardian|passage=Magnolias are some of the most primitive of our flowering trees, and fossils dating back '''millennia''' prove that they have had little need to evolve.}}
# {{lb|en|Christianity}} The period of one thousand years during which Christ will reign on earth (according to Millenarianist interpretations).
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1888
|author=w:C. I. Scofield
|chapter=The Seven Dispensations
|title=Rightly Dividing the Word of Truth (2 Tim. 2:15): Ten Outline Studies of The More Important Divisions of Scripture
|url=https://archive.org/details/rightlydividingw0000scof/
|edition=Second
|genre=Religion
|location=Philadelphia, Penn.
|publisher=w:Philadelphia School of the Bible
|year_published=1923
|OCLC=29679931
|page=25
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/rightlydividingw0000scof/page/25/
|text=After the purifying judgments which attended the personal return of Christ to the Earth, He will reign over restored Israel and over the earth for one thousand years. This is the period commonly called the '''Millennium'''. The seat of His power will be Jerusalem, and the saints, including the saved of the Dispensation of Grace, viz., the Church, will be associated with Him in His glory.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1911|author=w:Saki|chapter=Tobermory|title=The Chronicles of Clovis|passage=An archangel ecstatically proclaiming the '''Millennium''', and then finding that it clashed unpardonably with Henley and would have to be indefinitely postponed, could hardly have felt more crestfallen than Cornelius Appin at the reception of his wonderful achievement.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author={{w|Keith Thomas (historian)|Keith Thomas}}|title=Religion and the Decline of Magic|publisher=Folio Society|year_published=2012|page=137|passage=the end of the world would be heralded by a series of spectacular and symbolic events […]. According to most commentators, this '''millennium''' had already begun.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=w:Norman Davies|title=Vanished Kingdoms|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2012|page=117|passage=Conrad's later years unfolded in the shadow of the coming '''Millennium''', when the end of the world was forecast.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A period of universal happiness, peace or prosperity; a [[utopia]].
#* {{RQ:William James Varieties|lectures=XIV and XV|chapter=The Value of Saintliness|page=375|passage=But the aggressive members of society are always tending to become bullies, robbers, and swindlers; and no one believes that such a state of things as we now live in is the '''millennium'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1930|author=w:Olaf Stapledon|title={{w|Last and First Men|Last and First Men: A Story of the Near and Far Future}}|publisher=London: {{w|Methuen Publishing|Methuen & Co.}}|OCLC=43880808|passage=When rumour got afoot that in future mechanical power would be unlimited, the people expected a '''millennium'''.}}
# {{lb|en|with definite article}} The year in which one period of one thousand years ends and another begins, especially the year 2000.
#: {{ux|en|A huge fireworks display was put on in Sydney to celebrate the '''millennium'''.}}

